+PATCHED 15.3 — 05/10/2026
+Diagnostic build for Comment mode. The public commercial email is NOT
+restored, and this build was NOT validated against a real Instagram response.
+- Why 15.2 fails: Comment mode asks GET /api/v1/users/web_profile_info/,
+  whose email field data.user.business_email is null in every real capture
+  since 2022, and in the user's three real tests that request got HTTP 429 on
+  the first call. The flow that used to fill the email is
+  GET /api/v1/users/{id}/info/ -> user.public_email. It is still used by the
+  other modes and still excluded from Comment mode by the user's rule.
+- List first: the whole comment list is read and saved before the first
+  profile check, so a 429 on a check no longer cuts the list. A page without
+  a new cursor (missing or repeated) ends the list; in 15.2 a repeated cursor
+  kept the run from ever completing. On resume, commenters saved but not yet
+  checked stay saved even if the list stops early.
+- No inferred labels: business_contact_method CALL/TEXT with a null email is
+  an empty field ("Campo comercial vazio"), not "withheld by the web route".
+- No queue stop for missing emails: empty, omitted, hidden and personal
+  profiles never stop the queue; only access failures pause it.
+- Persistent profile cache (username + id; 14 days, 3 days for unavailable
+  profiles, 3000 profiles): no repeated request across extractions; cached
+  rows skip the per-row wait.
+- Adaptive spacing: 10 s base; each 429/400 doubles it (max 2 min) for after
+  the pause; five answered profiles in a row reduce it by 20%.
+- One-click diagnostic ("Verificar 1 perfil"): one request, then a card with
+  the route, HTTP status, Retry-After, the email-related field paths received
+  (names and value types only) and the result. The same paths go to the
+  diagnostic text and the XLSX diagnostic sheet.
+- Unchanged: request headers and cookies, the 429 pause and Retry-After
+  rules, no automatic retry in Comment mode, the serial lock, the 10 s minimum
+  spacing, no /users/{id}/info/ in Comment mode, no bio/site email.
+
